+# Islam page (`/[locale]/islam`) — sources, method and open review items
+
+Religious content lives in `lib/islam/*` (Arabic text, citations, counts). UI wording lives in `messages/*.json` under `islam`.
+**No religious text is translated**: Arabic texts and citations are shown as-is in every interface language.
+
+## Adhkar (morning / evening)
+- **Text source:** «حصن المسلم» (سعيد بن علي بن وهف القحطاني), chapter «أذكار الصباح والمساء», taken from the open
+  dataset `rn0x/Adhkar-json` (category 1, 24 entries). Orthography and diacritics are unchanged.
+- **Formatting-only changes:** removed the source's outer `(( ))`, the trailing count notes such as «(ثلاث مرات)»
+  (the counter replaces them) and the `*` verse-end markers; the basmala in the sūra entry was fully vocalised.
+- **Counts:** taken from the text of each entry. The dataset's `count` field was **wrong for «حسبي الله لا إله إلا هو…»**
+  (1 instead of 7, while the entry's own text says seven times) — corrected to 7.
+- **Periods:** entries whose own text restricts them (`إذا أصبح` → morning only; `إذا أمسى` → evening only) are shown
+  in that period only: #19, #20, #21 (morning), #23 (evening).
+- **Evening wording:** the source gives complete evening wording for #4 and #15 (used as the evening text) and only
+  partial/abbreviated evening instructions for #3, #6, #7, #16 (shown verbatim under the text, flagged in the UI).
+  Nothing was completed or reconstructed.
+
+### References verified while building (cited in the UI)
+| # | Dhikr | Reference |
+|---|-------|-----------|
+| 2 | Ikhlās + Mu'awwidhatān ×3 | Abū Dāwūd 5082, al-Tirmidhī 3575 |
+| 3 | أصبحنا وأصبح الملك لله | Muslim 2723 |
+| 4 | اللهم بك أصبحنا | al-Tirmidhī 3391 |
+| 9 | حسبي الله ×7 | Abū Dāwūd 5081 (mawqūf), Ibn al-Sunnī 71 (marfū') |
+| 10 | اللهم إني أسألك العفو والعافية | Abū Dāwūd 5074, Ibn Mājah 3871 |
+| 17 | سبحان الله وبحمده ×100 | Muslim 2692, Abū Dāwūd 5091, al-Tirmidhī 3469 |
+| 20 | سبحان الله وبحمده عدد خلقه… | Muslim, narrated by Juwayriyya (hadith number not recorded) |
+
+### Needs scholarly review (`review: true` in `lib/islam/adhkar.ts`)
+Entries with an empty `refs` list have **no verified takhrīj yet** and show «قيد المراجعة» in the UI:
+#6, #7, #8, #11, #12, #13, #14, #15, #16, #18, #21, #22, #23.
+Partially referenced, grading/hadith number still to confirm: #1 (Āyat al-Kursī — Qur'an 2:255 cited, hadith of
+morning/evening to add), #5 (Sayyid al-istighfār — Bukhārī, number to add), #19 (Muslim 2691 — confirm the
+morning-only wording), #24 (ṣalāt on the Prophet ×10 — grading is disputed among scholars; flagged `gradeDisputed`).
+
+## Pillars of Islam
+Names and the five Qur'anic references (47:19, 2:43, 9:60, 2:183, 3:97) are cited by reference only (no Qur'anic text
+typed by hand). Hadith of the five pillars: Bukhārī 8 / Muslim 16 (cited by reference; wording and order differ slightly
+between narrations). Explanations are short, general statements written for this site: **review recommended**.
+
+## Pillars of Salah
+Classification follows the **Hanbali school** (14 pillars, 8 obligatory acts) as in:
+- «دليل الطالب» (مرعي بن يوسف الكرمي) — summarised at islamqa.info/ar/65847
+- «رسالة في شروط الصلاة وأركانها وواجباتها» — محمد بن عبد الوهاب
+The UI states clearly that the schools differ (Maliki, Hanafi and Shafi'i count differently). Sunan shown are examples taken
+from the same source list, not exhaustive. Short explanations were written for this site: **review recommended**,
+especially for users following the Maliki school (common in Morocco).
